  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.4.1: Refresh NuGet listing and onboarding assets (rewritten README quickstart, recipes, compatibility/comparison docs, changelog) and update SourceLink dependency to remove NU1902 warning. 2.4.0: Add ExceptionAssertions.WithMessageMatching for wildcard exception message assertions. Add AssertionConfig.UseColorizedOutput to render expected/actual values in ANSI green/red for BeEquivalentTo member-mismatch diffs and Object/String Be/NotBe failures (opt-in, off by default). 2.3.0: Add SnapshotScrubbers (Guids/IsoTimestamps/Pattern/Combine) and a MatchSnapshot(scrub:) parameter to normalize non-deterministic values before snapshot comparison. Add StringAssertions.Subject public accessor (used by the new Swevo.AutoAssert.Json companion package). New companion package: Swevo.AutoAssert.Json (BeValidJson, HaveJsonProperty, HaveJsonPropertyEqualTo, BeEquivalentToJson for raw JSON strings with full structural diffs). 2.2.0: Add companion packages: Swevo.AutoAssert.Generator (compile-time, reflection-free BeEquivalentTo comparers via [GenerateEquivalencyComparer]) and Swevo.AutoAssert.AspNetCore (fluent HttpResponseMessage assertions for WebApplicationFactory/HttpClient integration tests). Core: BeEquivalentTo now consults a GeneratedEquivalencyRegistry fast path before falling back to reflection when both sides are an exact, registered type. 2.1.0: Add AssertionConfig.ConfigureEquivalency for process-wide default BeEquivalentTo options, and MatchSnapshot() snapshot/golden-file testing (serializes the subject to JSON and compares against a baseline file next to the test, auto-recording it on first run). 2.0.0 (breaking): Every assertion method now returns AndConstraint<T> for fluent chaining (.And.Method()...) instead of void. Added AssertionScope for collecting multiple failures into one exception. BeEquivalentTo now supports Excluding(...)/WithStrictOrdering() options and reports a full diff of mismatched members instead of stopping at the first. Added DateTime/DateTimeOffset/TimeSpan/Guid/Nullable<T>/enum/IDictionary assertions, execution-time assertions (ExecutionTime()/CompleteWithin), unsigned numeric Should() overloads, and many new string/numeric/collection/exception assertion methods. 1.1.0: Add BeEquivalentTo deep structural equivalence for objects, nested graphs, and collections with circular-reference protection. 1.0.1: Add missing package icon. 1.0.0: Initial release. Object, string, numeric, boolean, collection, and exception assertions.",
